                    "detail": "Baseline confirmed. Round-1 evidence shows a clean linear cost law: baseline 6 kernels → 15.36 µs, candidate-01 4 kernels → 10.24 µs, i.e. **2.56 µs per launch** for this 8192-element tensor. The bottleneck is purely kernel count, so a different direction than round 1 (which only removed the `clone`) is to collapse the chain itself.",
